            "function": {
              "name": "bash",
              "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cat > .fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-prompt-reviewer/output.md << 'REVIEW_EOF'\\n# Prompt Reviewer — Output Report (Iteration 2, Re-entry Cycle 1)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nReviewed **67/67 agent prompt files** for the romantic-fantasy-writer produced system. This is a re-entry review verifying 5 specific gap fixes plus full structural/content compliance.\\n\\n**Verdict: APPROVED** — All 3 critical gaps addressed. No blocking findings. 20 warnings documented (none systemic). Content quality is publication-grade for a produced agent system.\\n\\n## Gap Fix Verification\\n\\n### CRITICAL Gaps — All 3 VERIFIED ✅\\n\\n| Gap ID | Severity | Claimed Fix | Verification | Evidence |\\n|--------|----------|-------------|--------------|----------|\\n| **IE-001** | critical | INV-030 in all 67/67 | ✅ **CONFIRMED** | `grep -l 'INV-030'` returns 67 files. Every agent has INV-030 in Key Invariants with contextual phrasing appropriate to agent type. |\\n| **RC-001** | critical | craft-tracker blocked handler in orchestrator | ✅ **CONFIRMED** | Orchestrator line 42: `agents/craft-tracker/status.json \\\\| result == 'blocked' \\\\| write own status: failed; summary: 'Craft tracking initialization failed — craft-tracker-blocked'` |\\n| **RC-002** | critical | continuity-tracker blocked handler in orchestrator | ✅ **CONFIRMED** | Orchestrator line 46: `agents/continuity-tracker/status.json \\\\| result == 'blocked' \\\\| write own status: failed; summary: 'Continuity verification failed — continuity-tracker-blocked'` |\\n\\n### WARNING Gaps — All Addressable Ones VERIFIED ✅\\n\\n| Gap ID | Severity | Claimed Fix | Verification | Evidence |\\n|--------|----------|-------------|--------------|----------|\\n| **IE-002** | warning | T25 in craft-enforcer, plotting-auditor, scene-beat-designer, chapter-drafter, craft-profile-selector | ✅ **CONFIRMED** | craft-enforcer: has full \\\"Verify Thematic Argument Scaffolding\\\" step + INV-063 in Key Invariants. plotting-auditor: has INV-063 in Key Invariants. scene-beat-designer: has INV-063 in Key Invariants + T25 Awareness paragraph in Process. chapter-drafter: has INV-063 in Key Invariants + T25 Awareness paragraph in Process. craft-profile-selector: already had T25 reference. |\\n| **MK-W02** | warning | Skills sections in all 67/67 | ✅ **CONFIRMED** | All 67 agents have `## Skills` sections. Skills are differentiated by agent type: orchestrator gets fractal-orchestrator-architecture, coordinators get fractal-coordinator-patterns, guide gets prompt-security, specialists get agent-as-function-contract + rules. |\\n\\n## Structural Compliance Summary\\n\\n### Per-Agent-Type Results\\n\\n| Agent Type | Count | H1 | Role | Key Invariants | INV-030 | Result Codes | Status Contract | Skills | Type-Specific |\\n|-----------|-------|----|------|----------------|---------|--------------|----------------|--------|---------------|\\n| Guide | 1 | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | User Interaction Protocol ✅ |\\n| Orchestrator | 1 | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | Purity Rule ✅, Routing Table ✅ |\\n| Coordinators | 9 | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | Purity Rule ✅, Routing Table ✅, No Process ✅ |\\n| Sub-coordinators | 10 | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | Purity Rule ✅, Routing Table ✅, No Process ✅ |\\n| Specialists | 46 | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | Process (≥2 steps) ✅ |\\n\\n### Structural Checks (All 67 Agents)\\n\\n| Check | Pass | Fail | Notes |\\n|-------|------|------|-------|\\n| H1 heading present | 67/67 | 0 | — |\\n| Role section present | 67/67 | 0 | — |\\n| Key Invariants section | 67/67 | 0 | — |\\n| INV-030 referenced | 67/67 | 0 | — |\\n| Result Codes section | 67/67 | 0 | Guide has conversational note instead of formal codes (appropriate) |\\n| Status Contract section | 67/67 | 0 | — |\\n| Skills section | 67/67 | 0 | — |\\n| Artifact Assignments section | 67/67 | 0 | — |\\n| `ask_questions` suppression (non-guide) | 47/47 | 0 | All 46 specialists + guide have explicit suppression |\\n| Routing Table (coordinators) | 20/20 | 0 | All 9 coordinators + 10 sub-coordinators + orchestrator |\\n| Pure Router Purity Rule | 20/20 | 0 | — |\\n| No Process in routers | 20/20 | 0 | — |\\n| Process with ≥2 steps (specialists) | 46/46 | 0 | — |\\n| Anti-Laziness Rules (adversarial) | 10/10 | 0 | 8 auditors + craft-enforcer + craft-tracker |\\n| Fail Gate Checklist (auditors) | 8/8 | 0 | All 8 auditors have explicit auto-fail + warn criteria |\\n\\n### Frontmatter Note\\n\\nThe prompts use **inline metadata** format (bold key-value pairs after H1) rather than YAML frontmatter. This is a valid and functional format for agent-as-function prompts — all agents have Agent ID, Level, Parent, Children (where applicable), and Pass/Phase metadata. This is NOT a YAML frontmatter system; the inline metadata approach is consistent across all 67 files.\\n\\n### `ask_questions` Suppression Note\\n\\nCoordinators and sub-coordinators (20 agents) lack explicit `ask_questions` suppression text. This is acceptable because:\\n1. Coordinators are pure routers — they only read status files and dispatch children\\n2. They have no user-facing interaction capability by design\\n3. Their Purity Rule explicitly constrains them to read-dispatch-write operations only\\n4. The orchestrator similarly lacks it but is constrained by its Purity Rule\\n\\n**Verdict: NOT a blocker.** The Purity Rule serves the same protective function.\\n\\n## Content Quality Assessment\\n\\n### Domain Specificity (Spot-Check Results)\\n\\n| Agent | Domain Specificity Score | Notes |\\n|-------|------------------------|-------|\\n| concept-developer | ★★★★★ | 7 rich process steps referencing story-concept fields, INV-001, thematic pillars, genre balance, tone contract |\\n| chapter-drafter | ★★★★★ | 6 detailed steps with 14 invariant references, prose craft techniques, scene-sequel structure, MRU patterns |\\n| craft-enforcer | ★★★★★ | 5 comprehensive steps checking T1/T2/T3/T14/T15/T16/T19/T