        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "<overview>\nI am the **fractal-factory-checklist-validator** performing iteration 2 (re-entry) verification of a produced 67-agent \"romantic-fantasy-writer\" system. The task is to validate all 67 agent `.agent.md` files against structural and behavioral checklists, verify that 22 previously-identified gaps (3 critical, 19 warnings) were fixed, validate infrastructure (bootstrap script, schemas), and write a verification report. I built a comprehensive Python validation script, iteratively debugging it against the actual file format, and was in the middle of heightened scrutiny spot-checking when compaction occurred.\n</overview>\n\n<history>\n1. User requested checklist validation of 67 produced agent files for the romantic-fantasy-writer system (iteration 2, re-entry after gap-hunting cycle 1)\n   - Read all source-of-truth files: roster.json (67 agents), architecture.json, domain-model.json, gap-report.json, context.json, routing.json\n   - Most files were too large for direct viewing; used jq to extract structured data\n   - Confirmed 67 agents in roster match 67 .agent.md files on disk\n\n2. Built first Python validation script with YAML frontmatter parsing\n   - Script failed because f-string had curly braces issue\n   - Fixed syntax, re-ran — got 790 failures (44.6% pass rate)\n   - Root cause: agent files do NOT use YAML frontmatter; they use a different template format\n\n3. Investigated actual agent file format by reading sample files\n   - Read orchestrator, coordinator, specialist, auditor, and guide files (head -80 each)\n   - Discovered the template structure: H1 heading, bold metadata lines (`**Level:**`, `**Parent:**`, `**Children:**`), and H2 sections (`## Role`, `## Key Invariants`, `## Routing Table`, `## Process`, `## Anti-Laziness Rules`, `## Status Contract`, etc.)\n   - Cataloged all H2/H3 sections across all 67 files using grep\n   - Found 47/67 files have ask_questions suppression (all 20 without it are coordinators/orchestrator — pure routers)\n   - Confirmed 10 files have Anti-Laziness sections (8 auditors + craft-enforcer + craft-tracker)\n   - Confirmed INV-030 is referenced in ALL 67 files (critical gap IE-001 fixed)\n\n4. Verified the 3 critical gap fixes manually:\n   - RC-001 (craft-tracker blocked handler): FIXED — orchestrator routing table has `craft-tracker/status.json | result == 'blocked'` → failed\n   - RC-002 (continuity-tracker blocked handler): FIXED — orchestrator routing table has `continuity-tracker/status.json | result == 'blocked'` → failed  \n   - IE-001 (INV-030 not referenced): FIXED — all 67 agents reference INV-030\n   - IE-002 (T25/INV-063 missing from craft-enforcer): FIXED — craft-enforcer has `### Step: Verify Thematic Argument Scaffolding (INV-063/T25)`\n\n5. Built adapted validation script matching actual file format\n   - First run: 99.9% (1514/1516), 2 critical failures — V-CONSIST-01 and V-CONSIST-02\n   - Root cause: `Path.stem` on `x.agent.md` gives `x.agent` not `x`; needed `.name.replace(\".agent.md\", \"\")`\n   - Fixed, re-ran: 100% pass (1516/1516), 0 failures\n\n6. Per anti-laziness rules, 100% pass is suspicious — began heightened scrutiny spot checks\n   - Orchestrator: revision-loop handling confirmed, all result codes present\n   - Revision coordinator: all 5 children's codes handled with proper routing (including auditor retry logic)\n   - Guide: has User Interaction Protocol, INV-030, correct parent/children metadata\n   - Physical world coordinator: correct sub-coordinator chain (parent=worldbuilding-coordinator, children match)\n   - **FOUND ISSUE**: Auditor Anti-Laziness rules count was 0 for all 8 auditors when using `grep -c '^\\d\\.'` inside sed extraction — this means the script's counting method may have a false pass, OR the anti-laziness rules use a different numbering format\n   - This was the LAST action before compaction — the anti-laziness rules count discrepancy needs investigation\n</history>\n\n<work_done>\nFiles updated:\n- No files written yet to the repository — the validation report is at `/tmp/validation_report_final.json` but has NOT been written to the target paths\n\nWork completed:\n- [x] Read all source-of-truth files (roster, architecture, domain-model, gap-report, context, routing)\n- [x] Confirmed 67 roster agents match 67 .agent.md files on disk\n- [x] Discovered and documented actual agent file template format (no YAML frontmatter)\n- [x] Verified all 3 critical gap fixes (RC-001, RC-002, IE-001) plus IE-002\n- [x] Built comprehensive Python validation script with 27 checks per agent\n- [x] Ran validation: 1516/1516 checks pass across 67 agents + 2 global consistency checks\n- [x] Started heightened scrutiny spot checks (5 of N completed)\n- [ ] **INCOMPLETE**: Anti-laziness rules counting discrepancy found — grep shows 0 numbered rules for all 8 auditors, but script reports pass. Need to investigate whether rules use different formatting\n- [ ] **NOT DONE**: Infrastructure validation (bootstrap.sh completeness, schema docs completeness)\n- [ ] **NOT DONE**: Write verification-report.json to `.fractal-factory/verification-report.json`\n- [ ] **NOT DONE**: Write status.json to `.fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-checklist-validator/status.json`\n- [ ] **NOT DONE**: Write output.md narrative to `.fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-checklist-validator/output.md`\n- [ ] **NOT DONE**: Update `.fractal-factory/manifest.json`\n</work_done>\n\n<technical_details>\n### Agent File Template Format (Critical Discovery)\n- **No YAML frontmatter** — files do NOT start with `---` YAML blocks\n- Metadata is in bold key-value pairs: `**Agent ID:** A-002`, `**Level:** orchestrator`, `**Parent:** romantic-fantasy-writer`, `**Children:** agent1, agent2, agent3`, `**Pass/Phase:** concept`\n- H1 = display name (e.g., `# Session Orchestrator`)\n- Standard H2 sections present in ALL 67 files: `## Role`, `## Key Invariants`, `## Artifact Assignments`, `## Result Codes`, `## Skills`, `## Status Contract`\n- Type-specific sections: `## Process` (46 specialists), `## Routing Table` (20 routers), `## Pure Router Purity Rule` (20 routers), `## Anti-Laziness Rules` (10 agents), `## Pass/Fail Gate Checklist` (8 auditors)\n- Artifact Assignments format: `**Reads:** file1, file2` and `**Writes:** file1, file2` (colon INSIDE bold markers: `**Reads:**` not `**Reads**:`)\n\n### Regex Gotchas\n- `Path.stem` on `x.agent.md` returns `x.agent` — must use `.name.replace(\".agent.md\", \"\")` \n- Bold markdown `**Reads:**` needs regex `\\*\\*Reads?:\\*\\*` (colon inside bold), NOT `\\*\\*Reads?\\*\\*:`\n- The `get_section()` function uses heading level to determine section boundaries — works correctly for this template\n\n### Naming Convention\n- Prefix: `romantic-fantasy-writer` (from `context.json target.namingPrefix`)\n- Domain: `fantasy-writer` (from `context.json domain.name`)\n\n### Agent Hierarchy (67 agents)\n- 1 guide, 1 orchestrator, 9 L1 coordinators, 11 L2 sub-coordinators, 46 specialists (including 8 auditors + craft-enforcer + craft-tracker)\n- Orchestrator's 12 direct children: 9 phase coordinators + 3 cross-cutting specialists (continuity-tracker, series-kb-manager, craft-tracker)\n\n### Suspicious Finding Needing Investigation\n- V-TYPE-06 (Auditor Anti-Laziness >= 4 rules) passes in the script for all 8 auditors\n- But manual `grep -c '^\\d\\.'` on the extracted section returns 0 for all 8\n- Possible explanation: the anti-laziness rules may use a different format than numbered lists (e.g., `1. Rule` vs `### Rule N`) or the grep extraction boundary differs from the Python section parser\n- The concept-auditor.agent.md clearly shows numbered anti-laziness rules (lines visible in earlier file read), so this may be a sed extraction issue in the spot check, not a script bug\n\n### Gap Report Summary (22 gaps from cycle 1)\n- 3 critical: IE-001 (INV-030 missing from all agents), RC-001 (craft-tracker blocked unhandled), RC-002 (continuity-tracker blocked unhandled) — ALL FIXED\n- 19 warnings across categories: invariant enforcement, routing completeness, artifact coverage, test coverage, cross-reference integrity, bootstrap completeness, documentation completeness, meta-knowledge infrastructure\n</technical_details>\n\n<important_files>\n- `.fractal-factory/roster.json` (52.9 KB)\n   - Source of truth for all 67 agents: names, levels, parents, children, resultCodes\n   - Not modified; read-only reference\n\n- `.fractal-factory/context.json`\n   - Naming prefix (`romantic-fantasy-writer`), domain name (`fantasy-writer`), output directory\n   - Small file, fully read\n\n- `.fractal-factory/gap-report.json` (30.3 KB)\n   - The 22 gaps from cycle 1 that triggered re-entry\n   - 3 critical (IE-001, RC-001, RC-002) + 19 warnings\n   - Used to verify fixes in this validation pass\n\n- `.fractal-factory/output/romantic-fantasy-writer/agents/*.agent.md` (67 files)\n   - The produced agent system being validated\n   - Key samples examined: orchestrator, concept-coordinator, concept-developer, concept-auditor, guide, physical-world-coordinator, revision-coordinator, geography-builder, craft-enforcer\n\n- `.fractal-factory/output/romantic-fantasy-writer/bootstrap.sh` (322 lines)\n   - Creates directory tree, seeds artifacts (story-config.json, progress.json, manifest.json, continuity trackers, craft tracking, series KB)\n   - Has re-initialization guard, supports series-id parameter\n   - Partially reviewed; full infrastructure validation NOT yet done\n\n- `.fractal-factory/output/romantic-fantasy-writer/schemas/` (18 schema files)\n   - Schema documentation for all domain artifacts\n   - NOT yet validated against architecture.json\n\n- `/tmp/validation_report_final.json`\n   - Current validation report showing 1516/1516 pass (100%)\n   - Needs to be augmented with infrastructure checks and written to final path\n   - Contains full per-agent check details\n\n- `.fractal-factory/verification-report.json` — TARGET output file (not yet written)\n- `.fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-checklist-validator/status.json` — TARGET status file (not yet written)\n- `.fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-checklist-validator/output.md` — TARGET narrative file (not yet written)\n</important_files>\n\n<next_steps>\nRemaining work:\n1. **Resolve anti-laziness counting discrepancy** — The spot check showed 0 numbered rules for all 8 auditors via grep, but the Python script reports pass. Need to re-examine the concept-auditor (which was seen to have 5 numbered rules in earlier file read) to confirm the script is correct and the spot-check grep was flawed.\n\n2. **Complete heightened scrutiny spot checks** — Need more targeted checks:\n   - Verify a few more coordinators' routing tables cover all child codes\n   - Check `revision-loop` result code handling (coordinators emit it but orchestrator needs to handle it — there IS a wildcard handler)\n   - Verify the `Pass/Fail Gate Checklist` sections in auditors are substantial\n\n3. **Infrastructure validation** — NOT YET DONE:\n   - V-INFRA-01: Bootstrap creates directories for all 67 agents (partially verified — saw AGENTS array but didn't count)\n   - V-INFRA-02: Seeds universal artifacts (progress, manifest, context) — confirmed progress.json and manifest.json seeded\n   - V-INFRA-03: Seeds domain-specific artifacts — confirmed continuity trackers and craft tracking seeded\n   - V-INFRA-04: Re-initialization guard — confirmed (`if [[ -d \"${STORY_DIR}\" ]]`)\n   - V-INFRA-05: Every domain artifact has schema doc (18 schemas exist, need to verify completeness)\n   - V-INFRA-06: Schema field names match architecture.json\n\n4. **Write final output files**:\n   - `.fractal-factory/verification-report.json` — full validation report with all checks\n   - `.fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-checklist-validator/status.json` — status with result pass/fail\n   - `.fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-checklist-validator/output.md` — narrative summary\n   - Prepend entry to `.fractal-factory/manifest.json`\n\nImmediate next action:\n- Investigate the anti-laziness counting issue by reading concept-auditor's Anti-Laziness section directly\n- Run infrastructure validation checks\n- If everything passes, write all output files with verdict \"pass\"\n</next_steps>",
