ing by romantic-fantasy-writer-plot-architect'. Architecture.json says: writeProtocol='create-once', writers=['romantic-fantasy-writer-craft-profile-selector']. The designNote in architecture.json explicitly documents this was fixed for AC-002 but the schema file was never updated.\\\",\\n          \\\"recommendation\\\": \\\"Update craft-profile.schema.md: change writeProtocol to 'create-once', change writer to 'romantic-fantasy-writer-craft-profile-selector', remove all references to plot-architect. This fixes both the protocol mismatch and the ghost agent reference (audit oracle AF-ARTIFACT-01).\\\",\\n          \\\"reEntryTarget\\\": \\\"execution\\\",\\n          \\\"relatedAuditFindings\\\": [\\\"AF-ARTIFACT-01\\\"]\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"id\\\": \\\"AC-005\\\",\\n          \\\"severity\\\": \\\"warning\\\",\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"chapters/{N}/draft.md declared as create-once with 1 writer in architecture.json and chapters.schema.md, but roster.json declares 4 writers (chapter-drafter, pov-voice-maintainer, continuity-integrator, craft-enforcer) and all 3 additional agent prompts explicitly describe editing draft.md.\\\",\\n          \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"architecture.json: writeProtocol='create-once', writers=['romantic-fantasy-writer-chapter-drafter']. roster.json writes[] for draft.md: chapter-drafter, pov-voice-maintainer, continuity-integrator, craft-enforcer. Agent prompts confirm: pov-voice-maintainer 'verify and refine the POV character's voice', continuity-integrator 'edit chapters/{N}/draft.md to resolve [inconsistencies]', craft-enforcer enforces craft tool compliance. This is a genuine multi-writer artifact that should use read-modify-write protocol with clear ordering (drafter → voice → continuity → craft).\\\",\\n          \\\"recommendation\\\": \\\"Update architecture.json and chapters.schema.md to declare chapters/{N}/draft.md as 'read-modify-write' with 4 writers in specified order: [chapter-drafter (create), p