s + 3 explicit readers validated) |\\n\\n### New Gaps\\n\\n#### AC-004 [warning]: craft-profile.schema.md contradicts architecture.json\\n\\n**What**: `schemas/craft-profile.schema.md` declares:\\n- WriteProtocol: `read-modify-write`\\n- Writers: `concept-developer` (initial) + `plot-architect` (augmentation)\\n\\nBut `architecture.json` declares:\\n- WriteProtocol: `create-once`\\n- Writers: `['romantic-fantasy-writer-craft-profile-selector']`\\n- designNote explicitly documents why this is now single-writer\\n\\n**Root cause**: Cycle 1 fix (AC-002) updated architecture.json but the schema file was not regenerated.\\n\\n**Fix**: Update craft-profile.schema.md to match architecture.json: create-once protocol, single writer craft-profile-selector.\\n\\n**Related audit findings**: AF-ARTIFACT-01\\n\\n---\\n\\n#### AC-005 [warning]: chapters/{N}/draft.md create-once contract violated by 4 writers\\n\\n**What**: Architecture.json and chapters.schema.md say `chapters/{N}/draft.md` is `create-once` with 1 writer (`chapter-drafter`). But roster.json declares 4 agents writing to it:\\n1. `romantic-fantasy-writer-chapter-drafter` (initial creation)\\n2. `romantic-fantasy-writer-pov-voice-maintainer` (voice refinement)\\n3. `romantic-fantasy-writer-continuity-integrator` (consistency fixes)\\n4. `romantic-fantasy-writer-craft-enforcer` (craft compliance)\\n\\nAll 3 additional agents' prompts confirm they edit `chapters/{N}/draft.md` directly.\\n\\n**Root cause**: The creative-writing-coordinator dispatches these 4 agents sequentially within the drafting sub-pipeline. The architecture and schema were never updated to reflect this read-modify-write pattern.\\n\\n**Fix**: Change architecture.json entry and chapters.schema.md to `read-modify-write` with ordered multi-writer rules: drafter → voice-maintainer → continuity-integrator → craft-enforcer.\\n\\n**Related audit findings**: AF-ARTIFACT-02, AF-ARTIFACT-04\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Category 5: Test Coverage — CLEAN ✅\\n\\n### Methodology\\nRe-verified all 26 test scenarios in `test-plan.json` and all 26 fixture directories. Checked coverage across 5 dimensions:\\n\\n1. **Agent levels**: orchestrator (TEST-001/002/022), coordinator (TEST-018/019/022/026), specialist (TEST-016/017) ✅\\n2. **Pipeline passes**: concept (TEST-003), worldbuilding (TEST-005/016), character (TEST-017/024), plotting (TEST-023), drafting (TEST-004/008), revision (TEST-020/021), beta-reading (TEST-006/026), polish (TEST-022) ✅\\n3. **Error paths**: blocked (TEST-005/009/022), auditor rejection (TEST-003/004/023/024) ✅\\n4. **Re-entry**: TEST-007 ✅\\n5. **Convergence**: exhaustion (TEST-005/006), forced delivery/no-revision (TEST-021), delivered-with-gaps (TEST-022) ✅\\n\\n### Cycle 1 Gaps — All Resolved ✅\\n\\n| Gap ID | Status | New Test | Verification |\\n|--------|--------|----------|-------------|\\n| TC-001 | ✅ Fixed | TEST-022 | \\\"Delivered-with-gaps polish-coordinator blocked\\\" — covers orchestrator's delivered-with-gaps result code |\\n| TC-002 | ✅ Fixed | — | TEST-014, TEST-015, TEST-021 all now have fixture directories with 3 files each |\\n| TC-003 | ✅ Fixed | TEST-023 | \\\"Plotting-auditor rejection retry with sub-coordinator cascade\\\" — exercises deep retry |\\n| TC-004 | ✅ Fixed | TEST-024 | \\\"Character-auditor rejection with depth-3 cascade reset\\\" — exercises 7-status deletion |\\n| TC-005 | ✅ Fixed | TEST-025 | \\\"Series sequel production with series-kb influence\\\" — exercises sequelOf/seriesId |\\n| TC-006 | ✅ Fixed | TEST-026 | \\\"Parallel beta-reader fan-out with partial failure\\\" — exercises 2-level parallel dispatch |\\n\\n### Fixture Directory Audit\\nAll 26 directories (TEST-001 through TEST-026) contain exactly 3 files: README.md, context.json, expected-status.json. Zero sparse or missing directories.\\n\\n### Coverage by Category (10 categories)\\n- happy-path: TEST-001, TEST-002\\n- auditor-rejection: TEST-003, TEST-004, TEST-023, TEST-024\\n- convergence-exhaustion: TEST-005, TEST-006\\n- coordinator-routing: TEST-018, TEST-019, TEST-022, TEST-026\\n- cross-cutting-agents: TEST-010, TEST-011, TEST-012, TEST-025\\n- edge-case: TEST-013, TEST-014, TEST-015\\n- per-chapter-iteration: TEST-008, TEST-009\\n- re-entry: TEST-007\\n- revision-beta-loop: TEST-020, TEST-021\\n- specialist-behavior: TEST-016, TEST-017\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Category 6: Cross-Reference Integrity — DIRTY (2 gaps)\\n\\n### Methodology\\nComprehensive cross-reference scan across all produced files (152 items checked):\\n\\n| Check | Scope | Result |\\n|-------|-------|--------|\\n| Routing agent names → roster | 20 agents | 0 ghosts ✅ |\\n| Routing dispatch targets → roster | All children | 0 ghosts ✅ |\\n| Routing result codes → roster | All onResult entries | 0 mismatches ✅ |\\n| Architecture writers → roster | 44 references | 0 ghosts ✅ |\\n| Architecture readers → roster | 3 explicit references | 0 ghosts ✅ |\\n| Agent prompt names → roster | 67 prompt files | 0 ghosts ✅ |\\n| Schema agent names → roster | 18 schema files | **1 ghost** ❌ |\\n| Skill file agent names → roster | 5 skill directories | 0 ghosts ✅ |\\n| Skill result code table → roster | Result code table | **2 misattributions** ❌ |\\n\\n### Cycle 1 Gaps — All Resolved ✅\\n\\n| Gap ID | Status | Verification |\\n|--------|--------|-------------|\\n| CR-001 | ✅ Fixed | Zero ghost agent names in architecture.json or routing.json. All 44 writer + 3 reader references validated. |\\n\\n### New Gaps\\n\\n#### CR-002 [warning]: Ghost agent 'plot-architect' in craft-profile.schema.md\\n\\n**What**: `schemas/craft-profile.schema.md` references `romantic-fantasy-writer-plot-architect` as a writer. This agent does not exist in roster.json (67 agents checked).\\n\\n**Evidence**: Schema contains two references:\\n1. \\\"may be augmented during plotting by `romantic-fantasy-writer-plot-architect`\\\"\\n2. \\\"- `romantic-fantasy-writer-plot-architect` (may add tools during plotting)\\\"\\n\\n**Fix**: Remove both references,