## Methodology
For each category:
1. Re-run the same checks as cycle 1
2. Specifically verify each previous gap is resolved
3. Check the audit oracle findings relevant to your categories
4. Look for any NEW gaps not found in cycle 1
5. Document methodology, items checked, gaps found

## Output Requirements
Write your results to TWO files:

### 1. `.fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-infrastructure-hunter/output.json`
```json
{
  "version": 2,
  "timestamp": "<ISO8601>",
  "cycle": 2,
  "agent": "fractal-factory-infrastructure-hunter",
  "categories": [
    {
      "id": 7,
      "name": "Bootstrap Completeness",
      "status": "clean|dirty",
      "methodology": "...",
      "itemsChecked": N,
      "gapsFound": N,
      "gaps": [...],
      "resolvedFromCycle1": ["BC-W01"],
      "notes": "..."
    },
    { "id": 8, ... },
    { "id": 9, ... }
  ]
}
```

Each gap should have: id, severity (critical/warning), description, evidence, recommendation, reEntryTarget (planning/execution/verification)

### 2. `.fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-infrastructure-hunter/status.json`
```json
{
  "agent": "fractal-factory-infrastructure-hunter",
  "task_id": "pass6/infrastructure-hunting",
  "status": "completed",
  "result": "clean|dirty",
  "summary": "...",
  "artifacts": ["agents/fractal-factory-infrastructure-hunter/output.json"],
  "next_hint": null,
  "iteration": 2
}
```

Result is "clean" ONLY if all 3 categories have zero gaps. "dirty" if any gap remains or new gaps found.

Be thorough — check the ACTUAL files in the output directory to verify fixes were applied.
