json |\\n| story-concept.schema.md | story-concept.json |\\n| craft-profile.schema.md | craft-profile.json |\\n| world-bible.schema.md | geography, magic-system, politics, culture, history (5) |\\n| characters.schema.md | characters/index.json, characters/{CHAR-NNN}.json |\\n| romance-arc-design.schema.md | romance-arc-design.json |\\n| plot-structure.schema.md | plot-structure.json, dual-arc-timeline.json, tension-map.json |\\n| chapter-outlines.schema.md | chapter-outlines/{N}.json |\\n| style-guide.schema.md | style-guide.json |\\n| chapters.schema.md | draft.md, metadata.json, revised.md, final.md (4) |\\n| revision-reports.schema.md | developmental.json, line-edit.json, copy-edit.json (3) |\\n| beta-feedback.schema.md | 5 lens files + beta-synthesis/{N}.json (6) |\\n| audit-reports.schema.md | audit-reports/{phase}/{gate-id}.json |\\n| cross-cutting-trackers.schema.md | 6 tracker artifacts |\\n| delivery-and-series.schema.md | delivery-report.json, chapter-summaries/{N}.json, series-kb/index.json |\\n\\n**Result: All 42 artifacts have writers, readers, and schema documentation. Zero gaps.**\\n\\n### Secondary Observation (not a gap)\\n`plot-structure.schema.md` says `dual-arc-builder` co-writes `plot-structure.json`, but `architecture.json` and the dual-arc-builder agent prompt both say it only writes `dual-arc-timeline.json`. This is an incorrect writer attribution in documentation. It doesn't meet the Category 4 gap threshold (no missing writer/reader/schema) but is noted for completeness.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Category 5: Test Coverage — CLEAN ✅\\n\\n### Methodology\\nCross-referenced 26 test scenarios against 5 required coverage dimensions:\\n1. **Agent levels**: Every agent level (orchestrator, coordinator, sub-coordinator, specialist, guide) has at least one test\\n2. **Pipeline passes**: Every creative phase has at least one test\\n3. **Error paths**: blocked, failed, rejected scenarios are tested\\n4. **Re-entry**: At least one re-entry test exists\\n5. **Convergence**: Both convergence-exhaustion and forced-delivery are tested\\n\\n### Items Checked: 26 scenarios across 11 categories\\n\\n### Coverage Results\\n\\n**Agent Level Coverage:**\\n- ✅ Orchestrator: TEST-001, TEST-002, TEST-022\\n- ✅ Coordinator: TEST-018, TEST-019, TEST-022, TEST-026\\n- ✅ Sub-coordinator: TEST-018, TEST-019, TEST-023, TEST-024\\n- ✅ Specialist: TEST-016, TEST-017\\n- ✅ Guide: TEST-013, TEST-014\\n\\n**Pipeline Phase Coverage (all 9 phases):**\\n- ✅ concept: 12 tests\\n- ✅ worldbuilding: 5 tests\\n- ✅ character: 6 tests\\n- ✅ plotting: 3 tests\\n- ✅ style: 3 tests\\n- ✅ drafting: 6 tests\\n- ✅ revision: 6 tests\\n- ✅ beta-reading: 3 tests\\n- ✅ polish: 8 tests\\n\\n**Error Path Coverage:**\\n- ✅ Auditor rejection: 4 tests (TEST-003, TEST-004, TEST-023, TEST-024)\\n- ✅ Convergence exhaustion: 2 tests (TEST-005, TEST-006)\\n- ✅ Edge cases: 3 tests (TEST-013, TEST-014, TEST-015)\\n\\n**Re-entry Coverage:**\\n- ✅ 2 tests (TEST-007: re-entry from gap hunting, TEST-025: series sequel with KB influence)\\n\\n**Convergence Coverage:**\\n- ✅ Convergence exhaustion: TEST-005, TEST-006\\n- ✅ Delivered-with-gaps (forced delivery): TEST-022\\n\\n**Result: All 5 coverage dimensions satisfied. Zero gaps.**\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Category 6: Cross-Reference Integrity — DIRTY ⚠️\\n\\n### Methodology\\nPerformed 5 cross-reference checks:\\n1. Extracted all `romantic-fantasy-writer-*` references from 67 agent prompts, 18 schemas, and skill files → compared against 67 agents in `roster.json`\\n2. Checked all reader/writer shorthand names in `architecture.json` against roster, filtering collective terms\\n3. Verified cycle 2 fixes (CR-002, CR-003) are genuinely resolved\\n4. Checked result codes in orchestrator + coordinator routing tables against roster declarations\\n5. Second pass: audited 4 coordinator routing tables for result code consistency\\n\\n### Items Checked: 152 (67 prompt cross-refs + 42 artifact reader/writer arrays + 43 routing table entries)\\n\\n### Gaps Found: 2\\n\\n#### CR-004 [warning]: foreshadowing-ledger.json readers references non-existent 'plot-architect'\\n\\n- **File:** `.fractal-factory/architecture.json`\\n- **Location:** `artifacts.crossCutting` → `foreshadowing-ledger.json` → `readers` array\\n- **Current value:** `[\\\"plot-architect\\\", \\\"adversarial-auditor\\\", \\\"craft-beta-reader\\\", \\\"continuity-tracker\\\"]`\\n- **Problem:** `plot-architect` was dissolved into 5 specialists (structure-selector, dual-arc-builder, tension-mapper, chapter-outliner, scene-beat-designer) during depth analysis. `romantic-fantasy-writer-plot-architect` does not exist in `roster.json`.\\n- **Same root cause as CR-002** (cycle 2), but in a different location. The cycle 2 fix addressed `craft-profile.schema.md` but missed this entry.\\n- **Suggested fix:** Replace `\\\"plot-architect\\\"` with `\\\"craft-tracker\\\"` or `\\\"tension-mapper\\\"` (the agents most likely to consume foreshadowing data).\\n\\n#### CR-005 [warning]: mystery-box-inventory.json readers references non-existent 'plot-architect'\\n\\n- **File:** `.fractal-factory/architecture.json`\\n- **Location:** `artifacts.crossCutting` → `mystery-box-inventory.json` → `readers` array\\n- **Current value:** `[\\\"plot-architect\\\", \\\"chapter-drafter\\\", \\\"adversarial-auditor\\\"]`\\n- **Problem:** Same as CR-004 — `plot-architect` is a dissolved agent that doesn't exist in `roster.json`.\\n- **Suggested fix:** Replace `\\\"plot-architect\\\"` with `\\\"tension-mapper\\\"` or `\\\"chapter-outliner\\\"` (the agents most likely to consume mystery-box tracking data).\\n\\n### Clean Checks\\n- ✅ All 66 agent references in prompt files map to roster entries (0 dangling)\\n- ✅ All schema agent references map to roster entries (0 dangling, excluding bare prefix matches)\\n- ✅ All skill file agent references map to roster entries (0 dangling)\\n- ✅ Orchestrator routing table result codes match roster declarations\\n- ✅ Coordinator routing tables (concept, worldbuilding, drafting, beta-reading) correctly consume declared result codes\\n- ✅ CR-002 (craft-profile.schema.md plot-architect) confirmed fixed\\n- ✅ CR-003 (SKILL.md revision-required misattribution) confirmed fixed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n| Category | Status | Gaps | Items Checked |\\n|----------|--------|------|---------------|\\n| 4: Artifact Coverage | ✅ CLEAN | 0 | 42 |\\n| 5: Test Coverage | ✅ CLEAN | 0 | 26 |\\n| 6: Cross-Reference Integrity | ⚠️ DIRTY | 2 | 152 |\\n| **Total** | **DIRTY** | **2** | **220** |\\n\\nBoth gaps are **warning** severity (not critical). They are the last remnants of the plot-architect dissolution from the original depth analysis. The cycle 2 fix addressed the most visible manifestations (schema files, SKILL.md) but missed two entries in architecture.json reader arrays. A single targeted edit to architecture.json should resolve both.\\n\\n**Convergence assessment:** The system is converging well (22 → 6 → 2). These 2 remaining gaps share a single root cause and can be fixed in one edit. Expected cycle 4 result: clean.\\n\"}"
