              "arguments": "{\"new_str\": \"# Prompt Writer — Output Report (Iteration 4, Re-entry Cycle 3)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nCycle 3 re-entry: minimal fix for **2 remaining warning-level gaps** (CR-004, CR-005). Both were ghost references to dissolved agent `plot-architect` in architecture.json reader arrays. No agent prompts or other files modified.\\n\\n## Gaps Fixed\\n\\n### CR-004 — foreshadowing-ledger.json readers (architecture.json line 2060)\\n\\n**Problem**: Reader array included `\\\"plot-architect\\\"` which was dissolved in cycle 1 (split into structure-selector, dual-arc-builder, tension-mapper, chapter-outliner, scene-beat-designer).\\n\\n**Fix**: Replaced `\\\"plot-architect\\\"` with `\\\"tension-mapper\\\"` — the appropriate successor for foreshadowing-domain reads, as tension-mapper maps tension/foreshadowing arcs and needs visibility into the foreshadowing ledger.\\n\\n- **Before**: `[\\\"plot-architect\\\", \\\"adversarial-auditor\\\", \\\"craft-beta-reader\\\", \\\"continuity-tracker\\\"]`\\n- **After**: `[\\\"tension-mapper\\\", \\\"adversarial-auditor\\\", \\\"craft-beta-reader\\\", \\\"continuity-tracker\\\"]`\\n\\n### CR-005 — mystery-box-inventory.json readers (architecture.json line 2148)\\n\\n**Problem**: Reader array included `\\\"plot-architect\\\"` — same dissolved agent.\\n\\n**Fix**: Replaced `\\\"plot-architect\\\"` with `\\\"tension-mapper\\\"` — mystery boxes are a tension/pacing concern. `chapter-drafter` was already present in the array. `chapter-outliner` was an alternative but `tension-mapper` is the better domain fit.\\n\\n- **Before**: `[\\\"plot-architect\\\", \\\"chapter-drafter\\\", \\\"adversarial-auditor\\\"]`\\n- **After**: `[\\\"tension-mapper\\\", \\\"chapter-drafter\\\", \\\"adversarial-auditor\\\"]`\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n1. ✅ `plot-architect` no longer appears in any readers/writers array in architecture.json\\n2. ✅ Only remaining mention is in a `designNote` (line 540) documenting the dissolution history — correct to preserve\\n3. ✅ `romantic-fantasy-writer-tension-mapper` confirmed in roster.json\\n4. ✅ architecture.json remains valid JSON\\n5. ✅ No agent prompt files modified (minimal fix cycle)\\n\\n## Files Modified\\n\\n| File | Gaps Addressed | Changes |\\n|------|----------------|---------|\\n| `architecture.json` | CR-004, CR-005 | Replaced `plot-architect` → `tension-mapper` in 2 reader arrays |\\n\\n## Agent Prompts\\n\\nAll 67 agent prompt files remain unchanged — architecture-only fix cycle.\\n\\n## Previous Cycle History\\n\\n- **Cycle 1**: Depth analysis fixes, schema corrections\\n- **Cycle 2**: 6 infrastructure gaps (protocol mismatches, ghost agents in schemas, result code attributions, priority counts, Ralph reference)\\n- **Cycle 3** (this): 2 remaining ghost references in architecture.json reader arrays\", \"old_str\": \"# Prompt Writer — Output Report (Iteration 3, Re-entry Cycle 2)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nCycle 2 re-entry: all 67 agent prompt files were already approved (status `reviewed`). This iteration fixed **6 infrastructure gaps** identified by the gap-hunting pass across 5 produced output files plus `architecture.json`. No agent prompt changes were needed.\\n\\n## Gaps Fixed\\n\\n### GAP AC-004 + CR-002 — craft-profile.schema.md (ghost agent + protocol mismatch)\\n\\n**File**: `schemas/craft-profile.schema.md`\\n\\n**Problem**: Write protocol declared as `read-modify-write` with two writers: `concept-developer` and `plot-architect`. Architecture.json correctly specified `create-once` with sole writer `craft-profile-selector`. Additionally, `romantic-fantasy-writer-plot-architect` is a ghost agent — it doesn't exist in the roster (it was split into 5 specialists during depth analysis).\\n\\n**Fix applied**:\\n- Changed writeProtocol from `read-modify-write` → `create-once`\\n- Replaced two writers with sole writer `romantic-fantasy-writer-craft-profile-selector`\\n- Removed all references to non-existent `plot-architect`\\n- Updated README.md artifact table to reflect `create-once` protocol\\n\\n### GAP AC-005 — chapters/{N}/draft.md (writer count mismatch)\\n\\n**File**: `schemas/chapters.schema.md` + `architecture.json`\\n\\n**Problem**: `chapters/{N}/draft.md` declared as `create-once` with 1 writer (`chapter-drafter`). But roster.json declares 4 writers (chapter-drafter, pov-voice-maintainer, continuity-integrator, craft-enforcer) and all 4 agent prompts confirm they write to `draft.md` in a sequential editing pipeline.\\n\\n**Fix applied**:\\n- Changed writeProtocol from `create-once` → `read-modify-write` in `chapters.schema.md`\\n- Added 4-writer sequential pipeline documentation with roles: create → refine → fix → enforce\\n- Added Multi-Writer Rules section documenting the editing pipeline, version incrementing, and reset-on-retry behavior\\n- Updated `architecture.json` artifact entry: writeProtocol → `read-modify-write`, writers list → 4 agents, added `multiWriterRules` object with pipeline details\\n- Updated README.md artifact table to reflect `read-modify-write` protocol\\n\\n### GAP CR-003 — agent-as-function-contract/SKILL.md (result code misattribution)\\n\\n**File**: `skills/agent-as-function-contract/SKILL.md`\\n\\n**Problem**: Result code table misattributed `revision-required` to \\\"Beta-reading-coordinator\\\" (it's actually a data field from beta-synthesizer surfaced through the coordinator, not a coordinator result code). Also attributed `revision-loop` to \\\"Orchestrator\\\" when it's actually used by all 8 phase coordinators with the orchestrator consuming it for routing.\\n\\n**Fix applied**:\\n- Updated `revision-required` row: attribution changed from \\\"Beta-reading-coordinator\\\" → \\\"beta-synthesizer (data field in synthesis output, surfaced by beta-reading-coordinator)\\\"\\n- Updated `revision-loop` row: attribution changed from \\\"Orchestrator\\\" → \\\"All phase coordinators (8) — orchestrator consumes this code for cross-phase routing\\\"\\n\\n### GAP DC-W05 — README.md (priority count mismatch)\\n\\n**File**: `README.md`\\n\\n**Problem**: Priority level summary table showed P0=6, P1=14, P2=6 but test-plan.json has P0=7, P1=16, P2=3. Total (26) was already correct.\\n\\n**Fix applied**:\\n- Updated priority table: P0 → 7 scenarios, P1 → 16 scenarios, P2 → 3 scenarios\\n\\n### GAP MK-W03 — mcp-sidecar/SKILL.md (Ralph Orchestrator reference)\\n\\n**File**: `skills/mcp-sidecar/SKILL.md`\\n\\n**Problem**: Line 107 referenced \\\"standard in Ralph Orchestrator deployments\\\" — the produced system should be self-contained and not reference the factory infrastructure.\\n\\n**Fix applied**:\\n- Replaced \\\"standard in Ralph Orchestrator deployments\\\" → \\\"standard in multi-agent deployments\\\"\\n\\n## Files Modified\\n\\n| File | Gaps Addressed | Changes |\\n|------|----------------|---------|\\n| `schemas/craft-profile.schema.md` | AC-004, CR-002 | Protocol → create-once, sole writer, removed ghost agent |\\n| `schemas/chapters.schema.md` | AC-005 | Protocol → read-modify-write, 4 writers, multi-writer rules |\\n| `architecture.json` | AC-005 | draft.md artifact: protocol, writers, multiWriterRules |\\n| `README.md` | DC-W05, AC-004, AC-005 | Priority counts, craft-profile protocol, draft.md protocol |\\n| `skills/agent-as-function-contract/SKILL.md` | CR-003 | Result code attributions corrected |\\n| `skills/mcp-sidecar/SKILL.md` | MK-W03 | Removed Ralph Orchestrator reference |\\n\\n## Agent Prompts\\n\\nAll 67 agent prompt files remain unchanged — they were already approved (`reviewed` status) and none of the 6 gaps targeted agent prompts.\\n\\n## Template Compliance\\n\\nN/A for this iteration — no new prompts written.\", \"path\": \"/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/.fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-prompt-writer/output.md\"}"
