## Domain
The romantic-fantasy-writer is an autonomous multi-agent system that writes romantic fantasy fiction — from concept through worldbuilding, character development, plotting, prose style calibration, chapter drafting, adversarial phase gates, multi-pass revision, simulated multi-lens beta reading, and final polish. Designed for series production with shared series knowledge base.

## System Statistics
- 67 agents across a 3-level hierarchy
- 18 artifact schemas
- 9 skills
- 26 golden test scenarios
- 176 total files in the package
- Gap hunting converged at cycle 4 (22→6→2→0)
- Verification: 1326/1326 checks (100%)

## Your Job — Write Three Documents

### 1. Architecture Documentation (`ARCHITECTURE.md`)
- System overview and design philosophy
- Agent hierarchy (orchestrator → coordinators → specialists)
- Data flow between agents (artifact contracts)
- Workflow phases and their purpose
- Re-entry and convergence mechanisms
- Quality gates (invariants, auditors, phase gates)

### 2. User Guide (`USER-GUIDE.md`)
- How to install/bootstrap the system
- How to start a new story project
- How to configure story parameters
- Workflow walkthrough (concept → worldbuilding → characters → plotting → drafting → revision → beta → polish)
- How to resume interrupted work
- Troubleshooting common issues

### 3. Roster Reference (`ROSTER-REFERENCE.md`)
- Complete agent inventory organized by subdomain/coordinator
- For each agent: name, role, level, parent, input artifacts, output artifacts, result codes
- Cross-reference table showing which agents interact

## Write Rules
