  {
    "type": "function",
    "function": {
      "name": "task",
      "description": "Custom agent: Launch specialized agents in separate context windows for specific tasks.\n\nThe Task tool launches specialized agents that autonomously handle complex tasks. Each agent type has specific capabilities and tools available to it.\n\nAvailable agent types:\n- **explore**: Fast agent specialized for exploring codebases and answering questions about code. Use this when you need to quickly find files by patterns (eg. \"src/components/**/*.tsx\"), search code for keywords (eg. \"API endpoints\"), or answer questions about the codebase (eg. \"how do API endpoints work?\", \"what does this codebase do?\", \"where is authentication logic?\"). Answers multi-part questions thoroughly. Safe to call in parallel — batch related questions into one call or launch multiple in parallel. (Tools: grep/glob/view/bash/powershell, Haiku model)\n\n- **task**: Agent for executing commands with verbose output (tests, builds, lints, dependency installs). Returns brief summary on success (\"All 247 tests passed\", \"Build succeeded\"), full output on failure (stack traces, compiler errors). Keeps main context clean by minimizing successful output. Use for tasks where you only need to know success/failure status. (Tools: All CLI tools, Haiku model)\n\n- **general-purpose**: Full-capability agent running in a subprocess. Use for complex multi-step tasks requiring the complete toolset and high-quality reasoning. Runs in a separate context window to keep your main conversation clean. (Tools: All CLI tools, Sonnet model)\n\n- **code-review**: Agent for reviewing code changes with extremely high signal-to-noise ratio. Analyzes staged/unstaged changes and branch diffs. Only surfaces issues that genuinely matter - bugs, security vulnerabilities, logic errors. Never comments on style, formatting, or trivial matters. Will NOT modify code. (Tools: All CLI tools for investigation)\n\nUser-provided custom agents:\n\nThese are custom agents configured specifically for your environment. They may have specialized knowledge, tools, or workflows tailored to your project needs.\n\n- **agent-factory-explorer**: Explores the workspace to discover existing agents, skills, MCP servers, conventions, and infrastructure patterns relevant to building a new agent family.\n\n- **agent-factory-family-auditor**: Audits the full family and produces a local repair plan when the family still needs refinement.\n\n- **agent-factory-family-integrator**: Verifies whole-family completeness and assembles the pass-level family summary before the final family audit.\n\n- **agent-factory-orchestrator-auditor**: Audits the built orchestrator for purity, routing completeness, and correct control-file usage.\n\n- **agent-factory-orchestrator-builder**: Builds the top-level orchestrator once all component prompts and skills are ready.\n\n- **agent-factory-roster-architect**: Designs the family roster, workflow shape, skill inventory, and control-file queues before any implementation starts.\n\n- **agent-factory-roster-auditor**: Audits the family roster before any implementation begins.\n\n- **agent-factory-skill-architect**: Designs one required new skill at a time from the approved roster.\n\n- **agent-factory-skill-auditor**: Audits one skill at a time against its approved skill spec.\n\n- **agent-factory-skill-builder**: Builds one skill at a time from an approved skill spec.\n\n- **agent-factory-subagent-architect**: Designs one subagent spec at a time from the approved roster.\n\n- **agent-factory-subagent-auditor**: Audits one subagent specification at a time before it is built.\n\n- **agent-factory-subagent-build-auditor**: Audits one built subagent file at a time against its approved spec.\n\n- **agent-factory-subagent-builder**: Builds one subagent prompt file at a time from an approved spec.\n\n- **agent-factory**: Autonomous agent that creates complete agent-as-function families. Takes a description of what the agent should do and produces orchestrator, subagents, skills, and routing infrastructure.\n\n- **builder-implementer**: Implements one phase of an implementation plan — creates and modifies files as specified.\n\n- **builder-planner**: Parses phased implementation plans into a structured execution plan for the builder orchestrator.\n\n- **builder-reviewer**: Reviews implementer changes against the plan phase to verify correctness and compliance.\n\n- **builder-scribe**: Writes completion report summarizing plan execution results across all phases.\n\n- **builder-verifier**: Runs the plan verification checklist after all phases complete to validate end-to-end correctness.\n\n- **builder**: Autonomous orchestrator that executes phased implementation plans by dispatching subagents.\n\n- **fractal-factory-analysis-coordinator**: Coordinates Pass 2 (Analysis) — dispatches pipeline-architect, artifact-designer, and depth-analyzer sequentially\n\n- **fractal-factory-artifact-designer**: Designs shared artifact schemas, read-modify-write contracts, and data flow for the produced agent system\n\n- **fractal-factory-artifact-hunter**: Specialist gap hunter for categories 4-6: Artifact Coverage, Test Coverage, Cross-Reference Integrity\n\n- **fractal-factory-asset-auditor**: Audits existing skills, tools, templates, and agent infrastructure for reuse in the produced agent system\n\n- **fractal-factory-audit-oracle**: Audits the produced agent system against agent-as-function and fractal-workflow-eval perspectives, checking for contract drift and architecture violations\n\n- **fractal-factory-checklist-validator**: Validates produced agent files against the full structural and behavioral validation checklist, producing a verification report\n\n- **fractal-factory-context-signal-analyzer**: Analyzes process-level observations — agent performance, pipeline bottlenecks, invariant patterns — to extract learning signals\n\n- **fractal-factory-coverage-hunter**: Specialist gap hunter for categories 1-3: Subdomain Coverage, Invariant Enforcement, Routing Completeness\n\n- **fractal-factory-delivery-coordinator**: Coordinates Pass 7 (Delivery) — dispatches packager, documentation-writer, and report-writer sequentially\n\n- **fractal-factory-depth-analyzer**: Analyzes domain complexity to decide per-coordinator whether the produced system needs depth-2 or depth-3 hierarchy\n\n- **fractal-factory-discovery-coordinator**: Coordinates the discovery pass — dispatches domain-scanner, invariant-extractor, asset-auditor, and exemplar-analyzer sequentially\n\n- **fractal-factory-documentation-writer**: Writes architecture documentation, user guide, and roster reference for the produced agent system\n\n- **fractal-factory-domain-scanner**: Scans domain-brief and domain-docs to produce the initial domain model structure with subdomains for the fractal factory\n\n- **fractal-factory-execution-coordinator**: Coordinates Pass 4 (Execution) — runs prompt-writer → prompt-reviewer loop with retries, then dispatches infra-writer\n\n- **fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer**: Analyzes exemplar agent families to extract hierarchy patterns, naming conventions, routing idioms, and artifact patterns for reuse\n\n- **fractal-factory-factory-signal-analyzer**: Analyzes factory execution artifacts to extract domain-level learning signals about agent system production\n\n- **fractal-factory-gap-hunting-coordinator**: Coordinates Pass 6 (Gap Hunting) — dispatches 3 specialist hunters, aggregates their reports, and reports convergence or dirty state to the orchestrator\n\n- **fractal-factory-guide**: User-facing guide for the Fractal Factory — gathers domain context, builds context.json, and launches the session orchestrator\n\n- **fractal-factory-infra-writer**: Writes bootstrap script, artifact schemas, skills stubs, and golden test files for the produced agent system\n\n- **fractal-factory-infrastructure-hunter**: Specialist gap hunter for categories 7-9: Bootstrap Completeness, Documentation Completeness, Meta-Knowledge Infrastructure\n\n- **fractal-factory-invariant-extractor**: Extracts behavioral, structural, quality, and workflow invariants from domain documents and adds them to the domain model\n\n- **fractal-factory-knowledge-curator**: Curates accumulated meta-knowledge into a task-relevant brief for the Fractal Factory pipeline\n\n- **fractal-factory-knowledge-integrator**: Integrates learning signals into the persistent meta-knowledge store with strict quality gating\n\n- **fractal-factory-packager**: Packages the produced agent system into the target output directory, validates completeness, and produces a packaging report\n\n- **fractal-factory-pipeline-architect**: Designs the produced agent systems pipeline — passes, entry/exit conditions, and re-entry rules — based on the discovered domain model\n\n- **fractal-factory-planning-coordinator**: Coordinates Pass 3 (Planning) — dispatches roster-planner, routing-planner, and test-planner sequentially\n\n- **fractal-factory-prompt-reviewer**: Reviews produced agent prompt files for structural compliance, content quality, routing completeness, and anti-laziness enforcement\n\n- **fractal-factory-prompt-writer**: Writes .agent.md prompt files for every agent in the produced system roster, following the universal agent prompt template\n\n- **fractal-factory-report-writer**: Produces the final delivery report with coverage statistics, quality metrics, outstanding items, and recommendations\n\n- **fractal-factory-roster-planner**: Plans the full agent roster for the produced system — names, levels, parents, children, result codes, and artifact assignments\n\n- **fractal-factory-routing-planner**: Designs routing tables, re-entry rules, and convergence bounds for every coordinator and orchestrator in the produced agent system\n\n- **fractal-factory-synthesis-coordinator**: Coordinates the post-verification synthesis pass — dispatches signal analyzers and knowledge integrator in sequence\n\n- **fractal-factory-test-planner**: Creates golden test scenarios covering agent types, edge cases, re-entry, and convergence for the produced agent system\n\n- **fractal-factory-verification-coordinator**: Coordinates Pass 5 (Verification) — dispatches checklist-validator and audit-oracle sequentially\n\n- **fractal-factory**: Session orchestrator for the Fractal Factory — routes the 8-pass pipeline (Pass 0 + 7 + Synthesis), handles re-entry from gap hunting, manages progress state\n\n- **planner**: Researches change requests, asks clarifying questions, and produces specification, plan, and task breakdown files\n\nWhen NOT to use Task tool:\n- Reading specific file paths you already know - use view tool instead\n- Simple single grep/glob search - use grep/glob tools directly\n- Commands where you need immediate full output in your context - use bash directly\n- File operations on known files - use edit/create tools directly\n\nUsage notes:\n- Can launch multiple explore/code-review agents in parallel (task, general-purpose have side effects)\n- Each agent is stateless - provide complete context in your prompt\n- Agent results are returned in a single message\n- Use explore proactively for codebase questions before making changes\n- Use 'model' parameter to override the default model (18 models available)",
      "parameters": {
        "type": "object",
